# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# SpeakWise Environment Variables
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your values

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Gemini API — required for the real-time Gemini Live voice interview and
# for Gemini-multimodal audio transcription. NOT required for scoring /
# prompt-generation / concept-graph, which now go through OpenRouter.
# Get your key at: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OpenRouter — required for text chat completions (feedback scoring, prompt
# generation, concept-graph extraction). Pick any model from the OpenRouter
# catalogue at https://openrouter.ai/models; default is
# google/gemini-3-flash-preview which matches SpeakWise's legacy behaviour.
# Get your key at: https://openrouter.ai/settings/keys
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
VITE_OPENROUTER_API_KEY=your_openrouter_key_here

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Supabase Configuration (Required for cloud database)
# Get these values from: https://supabase.com
# 1. Create a project
# 2. Go to Project Settings > API
# 3. Copy the Project URL and anon/public key
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-id.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key-here

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Supabase Setup Instructions:
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 
# 1. Go to https://supabase.com and create an account (or login)
# 
# 2. Click "New Project" and fill in:
#    - Project name: speakwise
#    - Database password: (save this!)
#    - Region: Choose closest to you
# 
# 3. Wait for project to be created (1-2 minutes)
# 
# 4. Go to Project Settings (gear icon) > API
#    - Copy "Project URL" → VITE_SUPABASE_URL
#    - Copy "anon public" key → VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY
# 
# 5. Go to SQL Editor (left sidebar) and run the production schema file:
#    supabase/production_schema.sql
# 
#    This schema creates:
#    - institutions
#    - user_profiles
#    - instructors (compatibility registry)
#    - courses
#    - submissions
#    - student_history
#    - production-safe RLS policies
# 
# 6. Enable Realtime for tables (optional but recommended):
#    - Go to Database > Replication
#    - Enable for courses and submissions tables
# 
# 7. Restart your dev server: npm run dev
